 "caption": "A 252 × 198 rectangle is cut into squares: one of side 198, three of side 54, one of 36 and two of side 18. The last square, 18, is gcd(252, 198), and it tiles the whole rectangle.",
 "alt": "A rectangle 252 wide and 198 tall filled by a 198 square, three 54 squares, a 36 square and two 18 squares.",
 "description": [
  "Start with a rectangle 252 by 198, the numbers of the example.",
  "Cut off the largest square, 198 × 198 (252 = 1 × 198 + 54): a strip 54 wide remains.",
  "Three 54 squares fit in the strip (198 = 3 × 54 + 36), leaving a 54 × 36 piece.",
  "A 36 square fits once (54 = 1 × 36 + 18), leaving 18 × 36, which is exactly two 18 squares (36 = 2 × 18 + 0).",
  "The last square has side 18, so gcd(252, 198) = 18."
